    <item>
      <title>Sri Lanka vegetable prices rise 12% in Dambulla market</title>
      <link>https://example-agri.test/story/1</link>
      <description>Wholesale vegetable prices at the Dambulla economic centre
        surged 12% this week, driven by reduced supply of beans and capsicum
        following heavy rainfall in the North Central Province.</description>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Jun 2025 06:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>

    <item>
      <title>FAO warns of food-price volatility across South Asia</title>
      <link>https://example-agri.test/story/2</link>
      <description>The Food and Agriculture Organisation flagged elevated
        commodity price risks for South Asia amid drought conditions affecting
        key rice and pulse producing regions.</description>
      <pubDate>Tue, 24 Jun 2025 08:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>

    <item>
      <title>Monsoon onset delayed, farmers urged to adjust planting calendar</title>
      <link>https://example-agri.test/story/3</link>
      <description>The Department of Meteorology confirmed a two-week delay in
        the south-west monsoon onset this year. Agricultural extension officers
        are advising Maha season farmers to reassess sowing dates for Yala
        crops including bitter gourd and ridge gourd.</description>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Jun 2025 09:15:00 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>

